WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.920
I'm wearing a suit jacket, which can only mean one thing!

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.000
It's time for the Bank of Nerdfighteria's quarterly report.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.880
Or that I'm at a funeral,

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.100
but I'm not at a funeral!

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.700
So the Bank of Nerdfighteria has three branches.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.400
There's the executive branch, which probably has too much power,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.740
The judicial branch, which literally believes that corporations are people,

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.260
and then there's the legislative branch,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.140
which, presumably, was named ironically,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.900
since it hasn't passed meaningful legislation in nearly a decade.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.960
Wait! No, I'm thinking about a different institution.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.820
The Bank of Nerdfighteria's three branches are:

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.620
The giving branch,

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.760
the lending branch,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.160
and the spending branch.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.500
Let's start with the giving branch.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.940
The Foundation to Decrease World Suck, our actual, real life charity,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.360
has finished paying out well over a million dollars in grants from the 2015 Project For Awesome.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.580
The money went to all the organizations listed here,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.220
and it's doing lots of good all over the world.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.420
For instance, I recently heard from water.org

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.840
that Nerdfighteria has just funded a capped spring water well in Northern Ethiopia

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.760
that serves over two thousand people.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.640
So far, this year,

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.880
the Foundation to Decrease World Suck has just over seventy-three thousand dollars in the bank.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.280
Most of that money comes from 'vlogbrothers' ad revenue.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.760
Right now, half of this revenue goes to the Foundation to Decrease World Suck,

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.620
and half goes to sponsor education projects.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.740
So, thank you for watching the ad before this video!

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.940
Hopefully there was an ad...

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.440
Okay, let's move on to the lending branch.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.620
The Nerdfighter Kiva Group has now loaned more than 7.4 million dollars to entrepreneurs around the world -

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.040
also, more info about this in the dooblydoo -

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.080
but Kiva's made some important steps to improve outcomes with their partners lately.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.520
And then, Hank, there are two very exciting updates from the spending branch of our bank.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.620
So, in 2016, four CrashCourse videos have gone up each week.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.740
Like, currently, we're discussing:

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.260
literature,

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.300
the history of games,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:34.920
physics,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.660
and philosophy.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.740
But starting September first,

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:40.640
all the CrashCourse Patreon money raised for the remainder of 2016

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.520
will go to fund an expansion of CrashCourse in 2017.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.220
This will mean 5 videos a week by the spring of 2017,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.640
and hopefully 6 videos a week by the end of the year;

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:54.680
including our first forays into higher ed' topics like advanced physics and anthropology.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.380
And we're really excited to be growing more.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.260
Also, we're working to systematically translate CrashCourse videos into multiple languages.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.440
By the way, if you happen to have the talent and time to volunteer to help with that translation project,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.780
please let us know via the form in the dooblydoo.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.660
So, yeah, thanks to everyone's help on Patreon,

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.240
more Crash Course videos next year, available in more languages.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:12.820
And lastly!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:17.600
For more than a year now, Joe and Stan in our office have been working with help and funding,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.820
from Bill Gates' BGC3 organization,

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.480
to build out educational materials around Crash Course videos.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.740
Like, as you may be aware,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:29.580
textbooks are ridiculously, astonishingly, stupefyingly expensive,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.380
and we've always felt like maybe a better price for them

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.980
would be, you know, FREE.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.600
Because if high-quality curriculum materials were available for free online,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.500
it would allow schools to save money on textbooks,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.100
and invest that money in their most important resource,

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.200
which is teachers.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.480
So last week, Crash Course released its first full curriculum,

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.260
which covers AP World History,

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.220
with readings and primary sources,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.040
and assessment tools, for both students and teachers.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.320
Hopefully, it's like a textbook, plus worksheets and writing prompts,

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.900
except it's easily downloadable,

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.160
frequently updated,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.280
and free.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.680
You can find it all at TheCrashCourse.com,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.180
or there's a link in the dooblydoo below,

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.800
but we're really looking forward to getting feedback

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.980
from teachers and students,

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.620
so we can continue to update and improve the curriculum.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.540
This is just the beginning, and it's only one course,

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.140
but we're VERY excited about it, so please check it out;

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.440
share it with your teachers!

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.540
And hopefully we'll find funding to create more full courses in the future.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.580
I wanna, again, thank everyone at BGC3,

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.580
and also everyone who supports CrashCourse on Patreon.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.040
You can find CrashCourse's Patreon by clicking here,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.120
or there is a link down in the dooblydoo.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.040
There are lots of great perks available to Patrons,

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:35.100
although, by far, the biggest perk is knowing that, without you, CrashCourse literally would not exist,

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.220
so thanks.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.320
So that's the update from the Bank of Nerdfighteria!

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.780
Nerdfighters, if you have questions, I will be in comments.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.760
Hank! DFTBA! I will see you on Friday.

